      "duration": {
        "en": 14,
        "es": 16,
        "pt": 15
      },
      "prompt": {
        "en": "Why make ideas testable?",
        "es": "[NEEDS TRANSLATION]",
        "pt": "[NEEDS TRANSLATION]"
      },
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": {
            "en": "Testable ideas can be improved or discarded—if you can't test a belief, you can't know if it's wrong; untestable ideas can persist forever without improving or correcting",
            "es": "[NEEDS TRANSLATION]",
            "pt": "[NEEDS TRANSLATION]"
          },
          "quality": "best",
          "response": {
            "en": "Yes. Testability enables learning. If there's no way to be wrong, there's no way to get righter. Making ideas testable is making them improvable.",
